`static_assert` — Compile-Time Predicate (Pass Cases)
======================================================

Per reference §"`static_assert(cond [, "message"])`":

```sysl
struct EthHeader
    dst: [6]byte
    src: [6]byte
    ethertype: u16

static_assert(sizeof(EthHeader) == 14, "EthHeader must be 14 bytes")
static_assert(MAX_FRAME >= 64 && MAX_FRAME <= 1518)
```

- Module-scope compile-time check.
- Condition is evaluated by the constant folder (sizeof, comparisons,
  bitwise, shifts, arithmetic, refs to other `const` names).
- True ⇒ no code emitted.
- False ⇒ compile error citing the optional message.

This file pins **passing** static_asserts across all seven backends.
The asserts themselves emit no code, but their *presence* gates
compilation — if any one of them produces a wrong result through
the constant folder, the build would fail. After the asserts, a
small set of runtime tests confirms compilation actually succeeded
and the asserted layouts agree with the runtime sizes.

Failing-static_assert tests (`should_panic`-style for compile
errors) need a compile-error assertion mechanism in the runner that
isn't available yet — same gap as `trait_orphan_rule.lsysl` and
`contracts_off_flag.lsysl`. Deferred.

File-local prefix `Sap` (Static-Assert-Pass).

    module sysl.tests.lang_features


Basic equality on `sizeof`
---------------------------

    struct SapPair
        a: i32
        b: i32

    static_assert(sizeof(SapPair) == 8)
    static_assert(sizeof(SapPair) == 8, "SapPair must be 8 bytes")


Inequality on primitive widths
-------------------------------

    static_assert(sizeof(i8) < sizeof(i64))
    static_assert(sizeof(i64) > sizeof(i32))
    static_assert(sizeof(i64) >= 8)
    static_assert(sizeof(i32) <= 4)
    static_assert(sizeof(i32) != sizeof(i64))


Compound conditions
--------------------

    const SapMaxFrame = 1518
    const SapMinFrame = 64

    static_assert(SapMaxFrame >= SapMinFrame)
    static_assert(SapMaxFrame >= 64 && SapMaxFrame <= 1518)
    static_assert(SapMinFrame >= 64 || SapMinFrame == 0)


Arithmetic in the condition
----------------------------

    static_assert(sizeof(i64) * 2 == 16)
    static_assert(sizeof(i32) + sizeof(i32) == sizeof(i64))
    static_assert(sizeof([10]i32) == 10 * sizeof(i32))


Bitwise + shift in the condition
---------------------------------

    static_assert((1 << 4) == 16)
    static_assert((0xFF & 0x0F) == 0x0F)
    static_assert((0xF0 | 0x0F) == 0xFF)
    static_assert((0xAA ^ 0xFF) == 0x55)
    static_assert((1 << 10) > 1000)


References to other `const` names
----------------------------------

    const SapBaseSize = 64
    const SapDouble = SapBaseSize * 2
    const SapTriple = SapBaseSize * 3

    static_assert(SapDouble == 128)
    static_assert(SapTriple == 192)
    static_assert(SapDouble + SapBaseSize == SapTriple)


On-wire packet header layout
-----------------------------

    struct SapEthHeader
        dst: [6]u8
        src: [6]u8
        ethertype: u16

    static_assert(sizeof(SapEthHeader) >= 14, "EthHeader at least 14 bytes")
    // Some backends may pad to 16 — assert the un-padded payload is reachable.
    static_assert(sizeof(SapEthHeader) <= 16)


Runtime confirmations
----------------------

The static asserts above ran at compile time and emitted nothing.
These tests confirm the build reached runtime and the runtime sizes
match what was asserted.

### sizeof matches at runtime

    #test
    test_sap_compile_reached_runtime() -> unit
        assert(sizeof(SapPair) == 8, "compile + runtime agree")
        assert(sizeof(i64) > sizeof(i32), "compile + runtime agree")
        assert(SapMaxFrame == 1518, "const value preserved")

### const arithmetic survives codegen

    #test
    test_sap_const_arithmetic() -> unit
        assert(SapDouble == 128, "double")
        assert(SapTriple == 192, "triple")
        assert(SapBaseSize + SapDouble == SapTriple, "sum")

### packet header struct sizeof remains reachable from runtime

The struct's layout was already asserted at compile time via
`static_assert(sizeof(SapEthHeader) >= 14, ...)`. Re-confirm here
that `sizeof` agrees at runtime — the constructor itself isn't the
point of this category.

    #test
    test_sap_packet_header_struct() -> unit
        assert(sizeof(SapEthHeader) >= 14, s"got ${sizeof(SapEthHeader)}")
        assert(sizeof(SapEthHeader) <= 16, s"got ${sizeof(SapEthHeader)}")
